<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Phase 14 · Chevy Steamer — Bare Build Prototype</title>
    <style>
            *, *::before, *::after {
                box-sizing: border-box;
                margin: 0;
                padding: 0
            }

            :root {
                --coal: #0a0a0a;
                --coal2: #111114;
                --coal3: #18181c;
                --steam: #e8f4f8;
                --steam-dim: #a0bcc8;
                --steam-faint: #2a3a40;
                --ember: #ff6b2b;
                --ember-dim: #cc4400;
                --ember-faint: #1a0800;
                --iron: #7a8a90;
                --iron-light: #b0c4cc;
                --copper: #b87333;
                --copper-light: #d4956a;
                --brass: #c8a84b;
                --brass-dim: #8a6e28;
                --signal: #39ff14;
                --signal-dim: #1a8a00;
                --danger: #dc143c;
                --danger-dim: #8a0020;
                --text: #dde8ec;
                --muted: #6a8090;
                --font-display: 'Georgia',serif;
                --font-body: 'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;
                --font-mono: 'Courier New',monospace;
            }

            body {
                font-family: var(--font-body);
                background: var(--coal);
                color: var(--text);
                line-height: 1.6;
                overflow-x: hidden
            }

            /* ── BANNER ── */
            .banner {
                position: relative;
                background: var(--coal);
                border-bottom: 2px solid #1a2428;
                padding: 4rem 2rem 3rem;
                overflow: hidden;
                text-align: center
            }

                .banner::before {
                    content: '';
                    position: absolute;
                    inset: 0;
                    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% -10%,#ff6b2b08,transparent),repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,transparent 60px,#ffffff03 61px),repeating-linear-gradient(0deg,transparent,transparent 60px,#ffffff02 61px)
                }

            .banner-eyebrow {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 10px;
                font-family: var(--font-mono);
                font-size: 10px;
                letter-spacing: .25em;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                color: var(--ember);
                margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
                border: 1px solid #ff6b2b30;
                padding: 6px 20px;
                border-radius: 2px
            }

                .banner-eyebrow::before {
                    content: '';
                    width: 6px;
                    height: 6px;
                    background: var(--ember);
                    border-radius: 50%;
                    box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--ember);
                    animation: blink 1.4s ease-in-out infinite
                }
            @@keyframes blink {
                0%, 100% {
                    opacity: 1
                }

                50% {
                    opacity: .1
                }
            }

            .banner h1 {
                font-family: var(--font-display);
                font-size: clamp(2rem,5vw,3.8rem);
                font-weight: 400;
                color: #fff;
                letter-spacing: -.02em;
                line-height: 1.1;
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
                position: relative
            }

                .banner h1 span {
                    color: var(--ember);
                    font-style: italic
                }

            .banner-sub {
                font-family: var(--font-mono);
                font-size: 11px;
                color: var(--muted);
                letter-spacing: .15em;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                margin-bottom: 1.5rem
            }

            .banner p {
                color: var(--steam-dim);
                font-size: 14px;
                max-width: 860px;
                margin: 0 auto;
                line-height: 1.9
            }

            .banner strong {
                color: var(--ember)
            }

            /* ── LAYOUT ── */
            .wrap {
                max-width: 1400px;
                margin: 0 auto;
                padding: 4rem 2rem
            }

            .sep {
                border: none;
                border-top: 1px solid #1a2428;
                margin: 4rem 0
            }

            /* ── SECTION HEADERS ── */
            .eyebrow {
                font-family: var(--font-mono);
                font-size: 10px;
                letter-spacing: .22em;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                color: var(--ember);
                margin-bottom: .6rem
            }

            .section-title {
                font-family: var(--font-display);
                font-size: 1.8rem;
                font-weight: 400;
                color: #fff;
                margin-bottom: .8rem;
                letter-spacing: -.015em
            }

            .section-lead {
                color: var(--muted);
                font-size: 13px;
                line-height: 1.95;
                max-width: 1050px;
                margin-bottom: 2.5rem
            }

            /* ── METRICS STRIP ── */
            .metrics {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(140px,1fr));
                gap: 1px;
                background: #1a2428;
                border: 1px solid #1a2428;
                border-radius: 4px;
                overflow: hidden;
                margin: 2.5rem 0
            }

            .metric {
                background: var(--coal2);
                padding: 1.6rem 1rem;
                text-align: center
            }

                .metric .val {
                    font-family: var(--font-display);
                    font-size: 2.2rem;
                    color: var(--ember);
                    line-height: 1;
                    margin-bottom: .4rem
                }

                .metric .lbl {
                    font-family: var(--font-mono);
                    font-size: 9px;
                    color: var(--muted);
                    text-transform: uppercase;
                    letter-spacing: .14em
                }

            /* ── PIPELINE DIAGRAM ── */
            .pipeline {
                background: var(--coal2);
                border: 1px solid #1a2428;
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 2rem;
                margin: 2rem 0;
                overflow-x: auto
            }

                .pipeline pre {
                    font-family: var(--font-mono);
                    font-size: 12px;
                    color: var(--steam-dim);
                    line-height: 1.9;
                    white-space: pre
                }

                    .pipeline pre .em {
                        color: var(--ember)
                    }

                    .pipeline pre .sg {
                        color: var(--signal)
                    }

                    .pipeline pre .br {
                        color: var(--brass)
                    }

                    .pipeline pre .cp {
                        color: var(--copper-light)
                    }

                    .pipeline pre .dn {
                        color: var(--danger)
                    }

            /* ── GRIDS ── */
            .g2 {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(340px,1fr));
                gap: 1.5rem;
                margin: 2rem 0
            }

            .g3 {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));
                gap: 1.5rem;
                margin: 2rem 0
            }

            .g4 {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));
                gap: 1.2rem;
                margin: 2rem 0
            }

            /* ── CARDS ── */
            .card {
                background: var(--coal2);
                border: 1px solid #1a2428;
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 1.8rem
            }

                .card.ember {
                    border-left: 3px solid var(--ember)
                }

                .card.brass {
                    border-left: 3px solid var(--brass)
                }

                .card.signal {
                    border-left: 3px solid var(--signal)
                }

                .card.danger {
                    border-left: 3px solid var(--danger)
                }

                .card.copper {
                    border-left: 3px solid var(--copper)
                }

                .card.iron {
                    border-left: 3px solid var(--iron)
                }

                .card h3 {
                    font-family: var(--font-display);
                    font-size: 1rem;
                    font-weight: 400;
                    color: #fff;
                    margin-bottom: .8rem
                }

                .card p {
                    font-size: 12px;
                    color: var(--muted);
                    line-height: 1.85;
                    margin-bottom: .8rem
                }

                    .card p:last-child {
                        margin: 0
                    }

            /* ── BADGE ── */
            .badge {
                display: inline-block;
                font-family: var(--font-mono);
                font-size: 9px;
                letter-spacing: .14em;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                padding: 3px 10px;
                border-radius: 2px;
                margin-bottom: .8rem
            }

                .badge.ember {
                    background: #ff6b2b12;
                    color: var(--ember);
                    border: 1px solid #ff6b2b30
                }

                .badge.brass {
                    background: #c8a84b10;
                    color: var(--brass);
                    border: 1px solid #c8a84b30
                }

                .badge.signal {
                    background: #39ff1410;
                    color: var(--signal);
                    border: 1px solid #39ff1430
                }

                .badge.danger {
                    background: #dc143c10;
                    color: var(--danger);
                    border: 1px solid #dc143c30
                }

                .badge.copper {
                    background: #b8733310;
                    color: var(--copper-light);
                    border: 1px solid #b8733330
                }

                .badge.iron {
                    background: #7a8a9010;
                    color: var(--iron-light);
                    border: 1px solid #7a8a9030
                }

            /* ── STAT ROWS ── */
            .srow {
                display: flex;
                justify-content: space-between;
                align-items: center;
                font-size: 11px;
                padding: .4rem 0;
                border-bottom: 1px solid #0d1418;
                color: var(--muted)
            }

                .srow:last-child {
                    border-bottom: none
                }

                .srow .v {
                    font-weight: 600
                }

                    .srow .v.ember {
                        color: var(--ember)
                    }

                    .srow .v.brass {
                        color: var(--brass)
                    }

                    .srow .v.signal {
                        color: var(--signal)
                    }

                    .srow .v.danger {
                        color: var(--danger)
                    }

                    .srow .v.copper {
                        color: var(--copper-light)
                    }

            /* ── CALLOUT ── */
            .callout {
                display: flex;
                gap: 1.2rem;
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 1.4rem;
                margin: 2rem 0;
                font-size: 12px;
                color: var(--muted);
                line-height: 1.85
            }

                .callout.ember {
                    background: #0d0500;
                    border: 1px solid #ff6b2b20;
                    border-left: 4px solid var(--ember)
                }

                .callout.signal {
                    background: #020a02;
                    border: 1px solid #39ff1420;
                    border-left: 4px solid var(--signal)
                }

                .callout.danger {
                    background: #0d0004;
                    border: 1px solid #dc143c20;
                    border-left: 4px solid var(--danger)
                }

                .callout.brass {
                    background: #080600;
                    border: 1px solid #c8a84b20;
                    border-left: 4px solid var(--brass)
                }

            .callout-icon {
                font-size: 1.5rem;
                flex-shrink: 0
            }

            .callout strong {
                display: block;
                font-size: 13px;
                margin-bottom: .4rem
            }

            .callout.ember strong {
                color: var(--ember)
            }

            .callout.signal strong {
                color: var(--signal)
            }

            .callout.danger strong {
                color: var(--danger)
            }

            .callout.brass strong {
                color: var(--brass)
            }

            /* ── TABLE ── */
            .tbl-wrap {
                background: var(--coal);
                border: 1px solid #1a2428;
                border-radius: 4px;
                overflow-x: auto;
                margin: 2rem 0
            }

            table {
                width: 100%;
                border-collapse: collapse;
                font-size: 12px;
                min-width: 680px
            }

            thead {
                background: var(--coal2)
            }

            th {
                font-family: var(--font-mono);
                color: var(--ember);
                font-weight: 400;
                text-align: left;
                padding: .9rem 1rem;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                letter-spacing: .1em;
                font-size: 9px;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #1a2428
            }

            td {
                padding: .75rem 1rem;
                border-bottom: 1px solid #0d1418;
                color: var(--text);
                font-size: 12px
            }

            tr:last-child td {
                border-bottom: none
            }

            tbody tr:hover {
                background: var(--coal2)
            }

            td.ok {
                color: var(--signal);
                font-weight: 600
            }

            td.warn {
                color: var(--brass);
                font-weight: 600
            }

            td.crit {
                color: var(--danger);
                font-weight: 600
            }

            td.ember {
                color: var(--ember);
                font-weight: 600
            }

            td.copper {
                color: var(--copper-light);
                font-weight: 600
            }

            td.hi {
                background: #ff6b2b06
            }

            /* ── COST BARS ── */
            .cost-item {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr 100px;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 12px;
                font-size: 11px;
                color: var(--muted);
                margin-bottom: .8rem
            }

            .cost-track {
                height: 8px;
                background: #0d1418;
                border-radius: 2px;
                overflow: hidden
            }

            .cost-fill {
                height: 100%;
                border-radius: 2px;
                background: linear-gradient(90deg,var(--ember),var(--ember-dim))
            }

                .cost-fill.brass {
                    background: linear-gradient(90deg,var(--brass),var(--brass-dim))
                }

                .cost-fill.signal {
                    background: linear-gradient(90deg,var(--signal),var(--signal-dim))
                }

                .cost-fill.copper {
                    background: linear-gradient(90deg,var(--copper-light),var(--copper))
                }

                .cost-fill.danger {
                    background: linear-gradient(90deg,var(--danger),var(--danger-dim))
                }

                .cost-fill.iron {
                    background: linear-gradient(90deg,var(--iron-light),var(--iron))
                }

            /* ── TEST CARDS ── */
            .test-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));
                gap: 1.5rem;
                margin: 2rem 0
            }

            .test-card {
                background: var(--coal2);
                border: 1px solid #1a2428;
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 1.6rem;
                position: relative;
                overflow: hidden
            }

                .test-card::after {
                    content: attr(data-num);
                    position: absolute;
                    right: 1rem;
                    top: .5rem;
                    font-family: var(--font-display);
                    font-size: 3.5rem;
                    color: #ff6b2b06;
                    line-height: 1;
                    font-weight: 400
                }

                .test-card h3 {
                    font-family: var(--font-mono);
                    font-size: 11px;
                    color: var(--ember);
                    margin-bottom: .6rem;
                    letter-spacing: .08em;
                    text-transform: uppercase
                }

                .test-card p {
                    font-size: 12px;
                    color: var(--muted);
                    line-height: 1.7;
                    margin-bottom: .6rem
                }

                .test-card ul {
                    font-size: 11px;
                    color: #4a6070;
                    line-height: 1.9;
                    padding-left: 1.2rem
                }

                    .test-card ul li {
                        margin-bottom: .2rem
                    }

            /* ── REVIEW NOTE ── */
            .review {
                display: flex;
                gap: 1.2rem;
                background: #020a02;
                border: 1px solid #39ff1420;
                border-left: 4px solid var(--signal);
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 1.8rem;
                margin-top: 3rem;
                font-size: 12px;
                color: var(--muted);
                line-height: 1.9
            }

            .review-icon {
                font-size: 1.6rem;
                flex-shrink: 0
            }

            .review strong {
                display: block;
                color: var(--signal);
                font-size: 13px;
                margin-bottom: .6rem
            }

            /* ── SHIELD NOTE ── */
            .shield {
                display: flex;
                gap: 1.2rem;
                background: #0d0500;
                border: 1px solid #ff6b2b20;
                border-left: 4px solid var(--ember);
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 1.8rem;
                margin: 2rem 0;
                font-size: 12px;
                color: var(--muted);
                line-height: 1.9
            }

                .shield strong {
                    display: block;
                    color: var(--ember);
                    font-size: 13px;
                    margin-bottom: .6rem
                }

            /* ── TOTAL COST BOX ── */
            .total-box {
                background: var(--coal2);
                border: 2px solid var(--ember);
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 2rem;
                margin: 2rem 0;
                text-align: center
            }

                .total-box .t-label {
                    font-family: var(--font-mono);
                    font-size: 10px;
                    color: var(--muted);
                    text-transform: uppercase;
                    letter-spacing: .2em;
                    margin-bottom: .5rem
                }

                .total-box .t-val {
                    font-family: var(--font-display);
                    font-size: 3.5rem;
                    color: var(--ember);
                    line-height: 1;
                    margin-bottom: .5rem
                }

                .total-box .t-sub {
                    font-size: 12px;
                    color: var(--muted)
                }

            /* ── FOOTER ── */
            .footer {
                background: var(--coal2);
                border-top: 1px solid #1a2428;
                padding: 2rem;
                text-align: center;
                font-family: var(--font-mono);
                font-size: 10px;
                color: #2a3a40;
                letter-spacing: .1em
            }

            /* ── RESPONSIVE ── */
            @@media(max - width:700px) {
                .wrap {
                    padding: 3rem 1.5rem
                }

                .cost-item {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr 80px;
                    gap: 4px
                }

                .cost-track {
                    display: none
                }

                .banner {
                    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 2rem
                }
            }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- ═══ BANNER ═══ -->
    <div class="banner">
        <div class="banner-eyebrow">Phase 14 · Bare Build Prototype</div>
        <h1>The <span>Chevy Steamer</span><br>Stripped-Down Steam Electric</h1>
        <div class="banner-sub">Boiler · Dual Pistons · Rhombic Drives · Rail Engine · Hydrostatic AWD</div>
        <p>
            Phase 14 strips the system to its <strong>bare mechanical core</strong> — boiler, two dual-acting pistons with rhombic drives,
            sealed rail housing, oil-bathed engine, eddy exhaust sleeve, and hydrostatic output.
            Target: a working <strong>four-door sedan prototype under $20,000</strong> at standard wages.
            Every component is costed, heat-stress tested, and bench validated before fabrication.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ HEADLINE METRICS ═══ -->
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">Phase 14 · Key Targets</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Core build — stripped, costed, validated</h2>
        <div class="metrics">
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">$20K</div><div class="lbl">Target Build Cost</div></div>
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">2×</div><div class="lbl">Dual-Acting Pistons</div></div>
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">2×</div><div class="lbl">Rhombic Drives</div></div>
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">6</div><div class="lbl">Rail Wheels Total</div></div>
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">150</div><div class="lbl">PSI Max Boiler</div></div>
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">90</div><div class="lbl">PSI Min Floor</div></div>
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">AWD</div><div class="lbl">Hydrostatic Output</div></div>
            <div class="metric"><div class="val">H₂O</div><div class="lbl">Only Fuel</div></div>
        </div>

        <!-- ═══ PIPELINE FLOW ═══ -->
        <hr class="sep">
        <div class="eyebrow">System Architecture · Pipeline Flow</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Full system — boiler to wheels</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
            The complete energy chain from water in the boiler to rotational force at all four wheels.
            Steam does its work twice — once driving the pistons mechanically, once driving the rails via pressure.
            The rhombic drives harvest electricity from piston rod motion simultaneously.
        </p>

        <div class="pipeline">
            <pre>
<span class="em">BOILER</span> (rear of vehicle · vacuum-jacketed · 90–150 PSI)
    |
    | live steam
    ↓
<span class="em">PISTON A</span> ←————————————————→ <span class="em">PISTON B</span>  (dual-acting · rear · 180° phase offset)
    |              |                |              |
    | rod motion   | live steam     | rod motion   | live steam
    ↓              | pressure       ↓              | pressure
<span class="br">RHOMBIC</span>        |         <span class="br">RHOMBIC</span>        |
<span class="br">DRIVE A</span>        |         <span class="br">DRIVE B</span>        |
<span class="br">(electricity)</span>  |         <span class="br">(electricity)</span>  |
                |                              |
                | PTFE certified hose          | PTFE certified hose
                | (rear → front of car)        | (rear → front of car)
                ↓                              ↓
    ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │         <span class="em">RAIL HOUSING</span> (sealed manifold cover)   │
    │              steam environment only            │
    │                                               │
    │  <span class="em">RAIL A</span>  ←————————————————————————————→     │
    │           [W1]      [W2]      [W3]            │
    │                      |                        │
    │             <span class="br">[CENTRAL OUTPUT SHAFT]</span>           │
    │                      |                        │
    │           [W4]      [W5]      [W6]            │
    │  <span class="em">RAIL B</span>  ←————————————————————————————→     │
    │                                               │
    │  Steam pushes rails horizontally              │
    │  Rails push wheels → shaft rotates            │
    │  3 wheels per rail · 180° rail phase offset   │
    └────────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                             |
                             | [ROTARY SEAL — steam side / mechanical side]
                             | rotation only exits · no steam crosses
                             ↓
    ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │         <span class="sg">ENGINE HOUSING</span> (sealed · oil-bathed)      │
    │                                                │
    │   Input shaft enters oil bath                  │
    │   Oil smooths torque ripple from rail strokes  │
    │   Acts as torque buffer and accumulator        │
    │                                                │
    └────────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                             |
                             | clean smooth rotation
                             ↓
                   <span class="br">HYDROSTATIC PUMP</span>
                             |
                             | pressurised hydraulic fluid
                             ↓
          ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐
          ↓                  ↓                  ↓
     <span class="cp">WHEEL MOTOR</span>       <span class="cp">WHEEL MOTOR</span>       <span class="cp">WHEEL MOTOR</span>
     <span class="cp">FL</span>                <span class="cp">FR</span>                <span class="cp">RL + RR</span>
          └──────────────────┴──────────────────┘
                    ALL WHEEL DRIVE

<span class="dn">EXHAUST + RECOVERY LOOP:</span>
Piston exhaust → <span class="dn">EDDY COIL SLEEVE</span> (electricity) → RADIATOR → condensate → BOILER
Small 12V alternator off engine shaft → PCW + lights + valves (~150W total electrical demand)
</pre>
        </div>

        <!-- ═══ ENGINE INTERNAL DETAIL ═══ -->
        <hr class="sep">
        <div class="eyebrow">Rail Housing · Internal Geometry</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">How the rails drive the wheels — locomotive principle enclosed</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
            The rail housing takes the same reciprocating back-and-forth mechanism that gives a steam locomotive
            its enormous low-end torque, encloses it in a sealed manifold cover, and converts that horizontal
            reciprocating force into shaft rotation through six wheel contact points.
            Rails move. Wheels stay on the shaft and rotate. Steam stays inside the housing. Shaft exits clean.
        </p>

        <div class="pipeline">
            <pre>
TOP-DOWN VIEW — RAIL HOUSING INTERIOR

  STEAM IN (PTFE hose) ——→ [LEFT INLET PORT]         [RIGHT INLET PORT] ←—— STEAM IN (PTFE hose)
                                   |                          |
                         ┌─────────┴──────────────────────────┴──────────┐
                         │  MANIFOLD COVER (sealed · steam rated)        │
                         │                                                │
  ←————————————————————— <span class="em">RAIL A</span> ————————————————————————————→  (reciprocates)
                              [W1]         [W2]         [W3]
                                |            |            |
                           ═════╪════════════╪════════════╪═════  <span class="br">CENTRAL OUTPUT SHAFT</span>
                                |            |            |
                              [W4]         [W5]         [W6]
  ←————————————————————— <span class="em">RAIL B</span> ————————————————————————————→  (reciprocates · 180° offset)
                         │                                                │
                         └─────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘
                                               |
                                    <span class="sg">[ROTARY SEAL]</span>
                                               |
                                      OUTPUT SHAFT ——→ ENGINE HOUSING

  RAIL A pushes right  →  W1,W2,W3 rotate clockwise  →  shaft turns
  RAIL A returns left  ←  RAIL B pushes right (180° offset) →  shaft keeps turning
  Six contact points ensure continuous torque — no dead spots between strokes

  RAIL SURFACE: hardened steel · steam-compatible grease · no oil contamination possible
  WHEEL SURFACE: case-hardened · crowned profile · distributes contact stress
  MANIFOLD COVER: bolted cast iron · removable for service · steam pressure rated
</pre>
        </div>

        <div class="g3">
            <div class="card ember">
                <div class="badge ember">Rail Mechanism</div>
                <h3>Why horizontal reciprocation works</h3>
                <p>Horizontal rail motion is gravity-neutral — no energy lost lifting rail mass on return stroke unlike vertical. Steam pressure pushes rail forward, spring or counter-pressure returns it. At 90 PSI across a 60mm bore the force on the rail face is approximately 2,500N per rail — enough to produce meaningful shaft torque across three wheel contact points simultaneously.</p>
                <div class="srow"><span>Rail travel per stroke</span><span class="v ember">120mm</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Force per rail at 90 PSI</span><span class="v ember">~2,500N</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Force per rail at 150 PSI</span><span class="v ember">~4,100N</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Wheel contact points</span><span class="v brass">3 per rail · 6 total</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Phase offset Rail A vs B</span><span class="v signal">180°</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Rail surface material</span><span class="v copper">Hardened 52100 steel</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="card brass">
                <div class="badge brass">Rotary Seal</div>
                <h3>The steam-to-mechanical barrier</h3>
                <p>The output shaft exits the rail housing through a rotary lip seal rated for steam temperature and pressure. This is a standard engineering solution — identical in principle to a crankshaft rear main seal but rated for wet steam rather than oil. Steam stays inside the rail housing. The shaft carries only rotation into the engine housing. No cross-contamination is possible at this interface.</p>
                <div class="srow"><span>Seal type</span><span class="v brass">PTFE lip · spring-loaded</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Steam rating</span><span class="v ember">200°C · 200 PSI</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Shaft surface finish</span><span class="v signal">Ra 0.4μm ground</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Replacement interval</span><span class="v brass">15,000 miles</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Failure mode</span><span class="v copper">Steam weep (visible · safe)</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="card signal">
                <div class="badge signal">Rhombic Drives</div>
                <h3>Electricity from piston rod motion</h3>
                <p>Each piston's connecting rod drives a rhombic crank simultaneously with pushing steam pressure forward. Zero side thrust on piston walls. Counter-rotating cranks cancel all lateral load. Output shaft couples to a small generator or directly charges the 12V system via rectifier. Phase 14 bench test T-2 determines whether rhombic output alone covers the ~150W electrical demand or whether a small supplementary generator is needed at the front.</p>
                <div class="srow"><span>Expected output each</span><span class="v signal">~400–900W gross</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>After 20% margin</span><span class="v signal">~320–720W each</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Both combined</span><span class="v signal">~640–1,440W</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Electrical demand</span><span class="v brass">~150W (PCW+lights+valves)</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Surplus to 12V battery</span><span class="v signal">Significant — charges fast</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Fallback if insufficient</span><span class="v ember">Small front alternator</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ═══ BOILER SAFETY + SHIELD ═══ -->
        <hr class="sep">
        <div class="eyebrow">Safety Architecture · Boiler Protection</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Boiler shield, pressure relief, and safety stack</h2>

        <div class="shield">
            <div style="font-size:1.6rem;flex-shrink:0">🛡️</div>
            <div>
                <strong>Blast Shield — Armour Plate Behind Boiler</strong>
                A 6mm AR400 abrasion-resistant steel plate mounts between the boiler and the passenger compartment on the firewall.
                AR400 is used in mining equipment impact liners — it absorbs and distributes shockwave energy rather than fragmenting.
                At the target vehicle weight (~1,500kg Impala class) a 6mm plate covering 600×400mm weighs approximately 11kg — acceptable.
                A boiler rupture at 150 PSI would vent steam rearward and outward — the plate redirects that energy away from occupants.
                Combined with the ASME pressure vessel rating, three independent pressure relief valves, and PCW pressure monitoring,
                the probability of uncontained rupture is extremely low. The shield is the last-resort passive protection layer.
                <div style="margin-top:.8rem;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.4rem;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">
                    <span>Shield material: AR400 steel</span><span>Thickness: 6mm</span>
                    <span>Coverage area: 600×400mm</span><span>Weight penalty: ~11kg</span>
                    <span>Relief valves: 3× independent</span><span>PCW pressure cutoff: 155 PSI</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="g2">
            <div class="card danger">
                <div class="badge danger">Pressure Relief Stack</div>
                <h3>Three independent layers before rupture</h3>
                <div class="srow"><span>Layer 1 — PCW electronic cutoff</span><span class="v signal">Cuts heater at 150 PSI</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Layer 2 — Mechanical PRV</span><span class="v brass">Springs open at 155 PSI</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Layer 3 — Fusible plug</span><span class="v danger">Melts at 230°C (overtemp)</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Boiler burst test rating</span><span class="v signal">340 PSI (2.27× working)</span></div>
                <div class="srow"><span>Annual inspection required</span><span class="v brass">ASME inspector · yes</span></div>
                <p style="margin-top:.8rem">All three relief layers must fail simultaneously for any rupture risk. Probability is comparable to a conventional car fuel tank fire — rare with proper maintenance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card ember">
                <div class="badge ember">Boiler Specification</div>
