        <!-- ═══ BENCH TESTS ═══ -->
        <hr class="sep">
        <div class="eyebrow">Phase 14 · Bench Test Schedule — 8 Tests</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Nothing advances to vehicle installation without a passing bench result</h2>

        <div class="test-grid">
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T1">
                <div class="badge ember">Priority ①</div>
                <h3>T-1 · Boiler Pressure + Vacuum Test</h3>
                <p>Validate the ASME inner vessel and vacuum jacket before any steam operation.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Hydrostatic test inner vessel to 225 PSI · hold 30 minutes · no drop</li>
                    <li>Vacuum jacket: achieve &lt;10 mTorr · thermal loss must be &lt;40% of non-jacketed</li>
                    <li>Heat-up test: 2,000W heater · cold to 90 PSI · must be &lt;55 minutes</li>
                    <li>Pressure decay: hold 90 PSI heater off · &lt;5 PSI drop per hour</li>
                    <li>All 3 PRVs tested: must open at 155 PSI ±5 PSI</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: holds 225 PSI · vacuum achieved · heat-up &lt;55 min · PRVs open correctly</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T2">
                <div class="badge brass">Priority ②</div>
                <h3>T-2 · Dual-Acting Piston Steam Test</h3>
                <p>Validate piston sealing, force output, and dual-acting pressure on both sides of cylinder.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Feed steam at 90 PSI · measure force output on piston rod via load cell</li>
                    <li>Feed steam at 150 PSI · confirm linear force increase</li>
                    <li>Cycle 500 continuous strokes · check ring seal integrity after</li>
                    <li>Measure stuffing box seal leak rate · must be zero at 90 PSI</li>
                    <li>Confirm dual-acting: both forward and return strokes produce measurable force</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: force within 10% of calculated · zero stuffing box leak · rings intact</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T3">
                <div class="badge ember">Priority ③</div>
                <h3>T-3 · Rhombic Drive + Alternator Output</h3>
                <p>Confirm rhombic drive geometry and electrical output from both alternators under piston steam input.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Lateral force measurement: strain gauge on piston rod · must be &lt;50N side force</li>
                    <li>Connect both alternators to 12V load bank · measure combined output</li>
                    <li>At 90 PSI: target ≥300W combined after rectification</li>
                    <li>At 150 PSI: target ≥600W combined</li>
                    <li>Run 30 minutes sustained: alternator winding temp must stay &lt;100°C</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: &lt;50N side force · ≥300W at 90 PSI · &lt;100°C windings</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T4">
                <div class="badge brass">Priority ④</div>
                <h3>T-4 · Steam Line Pressure + Life Test</h3>
                <p>Validate PTFE hose and fittings under sustained steam pressure and thermal cycling.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Pressure cycle: 0→150 PSI · 10,000 cycles · no leak or delamination</li>
                    <li>Temperature cycle: 25°C→200°C · 500 cycles · inspect fittings after</li>
                    <li>Burst pressure after cycling: must exceed 400 PSI</li>
                    <li>Aerogel wrap: measure heat retention vs unwrapped at 150 PSI steam</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: burst &gt;400 PSI · no fitting fretting · aerogel retains &gt;30% heat</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T5">
                <div class="badge ember">Priority ⑤</div>
                <h3>T-5 · Rail Housing + Rotary Seal Test</h3>
                <p>Validate rail reciprocation, wheel contact force, shaft output torque, and seal integrity under steam.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Feed steam at 90 PSI to rail housing inlet ports · measure shaft output torque</li>
                    <li>Confirm 180° phase offset between Rail A and Rail B produces continuous shaft rotation</li>
                    <li>Run 1,000 continuous rail cycles · measure rail surface wear with profilometer</li>
                    <li>Rotary seal: inspect for steam weep after 1,000 cycles · none acceptable at 90 PSI</li>
                    <li>Shaft output: torque ripple must be &lt;10% peak-to-peak</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: continuous rotation confirmed · &lt;10% ripple · zero seal weep</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T6">
                <div class="badge brass">Priority ⑥</div>
                <h3>T-6 · Engine Housing + Hydrostatic Endurance</h3>
                <p>Full drivetrain endurance: shaft input → engine oil bath → hydrostatic pump → wheel motors.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Run combined system for 4 hours at simulated cruise shaft speed</li>
                    <li>Engine oil temperature: must stay &lt;120°C throughout</li>
                    <li>Hydraulic fluid temperature: must stay &lt;80°C throughout</li>
                    <li>All 4 wheel motor outputs: measure torque balance · must be within 5% of each other</li>
                    <li>Check for hydraulic leaks at all JIC fittings after 4-hour run</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: temps in limits · balanced wheel output · zero leaks</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T7">
                <div class="badge ember">Priority ⑦</div>
                <h3>T-7 · Eddy Coil Exhaust Sleeve</h3>
                <p>Validate electrical output from exhaust steam sleeve before vehicle installation.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Route exhaust steam at 120–180°C through 300mm ceramic sleeve</li>
                    <li>Measure output at idle exhaust flow: target ≥150W</li>
                    <li>Thermal soak 4 hours at 200°C: check coil insulation integrity &gt;100 MΩ</li>
                    <li>Back-pressure check: must add &lt;2% resistance to exhaust flow</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: ≥150W output · &gt;100 MΩ insulation · &lt;2% back-pressure</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="test-card" data-num="T8">
                <div class="badge brass">Priority ⑧</div>
                <h3>T-8 · PCW Firmware + Safety Stack</h3>
                <p>Validate PCW pressure floor enforcement, throttle control, and all failsafe pathways.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Simulate throttle sweep: PCW must never command below 90 PSI</li>
                    <li>Simulate pressure transducer failure: PCW must hold last known good value and alert</li>
                    <li>Overpressure test: simulate 155 PSI reading · PCW must cut heater within 200ms</li>
                    <li>Watchdog timer: force CPU halt · hardware must de-energise throttle valve</li>
                    <li>Eddy coil + rhombic outputs: PCW must log and display both channels</li>
                    <li>Pass/fail: PSI floor never breached · all failsafes trigger correctly · &lt;200ms response</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

